{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3oyFfP3CdHi99X1sXcNt9","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:95:Window size $k{=}5$ is optimal; $k{=}3$ drops 5.9\\,pp, $k{=}7$ drops 1.8\\,pp (Appendix Table~\\ref{tab:window_ablation}).\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:40:\\caption{Window size ablation on SWE-Agent conf${\\geq}$2 using the Qwen3-0.6B encoder (seed~42). $k{=}5$ is optimal. $k{=}3$ lacks sufficient context for stagnation detection (F1\\textsubscript{stag} drops 11.3\\,pp). $k{=}7$ dilutes signal by spanning both progress and stagnation phases.}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012NX7ee5aKMp69d7sggVgGk","session_id":"a13beb9d-44fb-4973-a348-fa71d68014d3","uuid":"f074cd27-a1f0-465e-aebf-c713043c8c37","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:12:49.908Z"}
