{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sjwwu7LgJXyMGBfihwnzyt","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/acl.sty:309:  % This is necessary because \\href command is used in the acl_natbib.bst file.\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_latex.tex:20:% This is not strictly necessary, and may be commented out,\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_latex.tex:25:% This is also not strictly necessary, and may be commented out.\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl.sty:309:  % This is necessary because \\href command is used in the acl_natbib.bst file.\ndocs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:16:\\citet{orlanski2026slopcodebench} document coding agent degradation; \\citet{chen2025monitoring} show sequence-level context is necessary; \\citet{kale2025weaktostrong} show weak monitors can oversee stronger agents; and \\citet{cemri2025multiagentfail,zhu2025agentfail} catalog systematic failure modes.\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:147:Three CS graduate students annotate a stratified gold set; 512 windows received at least one annotation, with Set~B ($N{=}505$, ${\\geq}$2 annotators agree) as the primary evaluation (protocol and IAA in Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_gold_set}).\ndocs/paper/sections/method.tex:51:Uses the final task outcome as distant supervision: unresolved tasks' last windows receive stagnation votes; resolved tasks receive progress votes; all others abstain.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:310:Missed stagnation windows (FN) are not borderline cases---the model assigns them a mean stagnation probability of only 0.078 (i.e., high progress confidence of 0.922), with 73\\% receiving $>$0.9 progress probability.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:376:Of these, 512 received at least one annotation.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:379:Annotators receive the $k{=}5$ action descriptions with full command outputs and file diffs, but \\emph{not} the task outcome (resolved/unresolved), preventing information leakage from $\\lambda_3$.\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:5:As these deployments scale, a critical failure mode has emerged that is qualitatively different from crashes or syntax errors: the agent \\emph{stagnates}---continuing to produce actions that appear purposeful while making no meaningful progress toward the task goal.\ndocs/paper/acl_natbib.bst:381:FUNCTION {tie.or.space.prefix} % puts ~ before the preceding part if it is of length <3\ndocs/paper/acl_natbib.bst:470:MACRO {dec} {\"December\"}\ndocs/paper/acl_natbib.bst:1099:FUNCTION {archiveprefix.or.eprinttype} % holder for eprinttype with archiveprefix precedence\ndocs/paper/acl_natbib.bst:1128:            { journal } % if journal field is not empty, output it (takes precedence)\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_natbib.bst:381:FUNCTION {tie.or.space.prefix} % puts ~ before the preceding part if it is of length <3\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_natbib.bst:470:MACRO {dec} {\"December\"}\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_natbib.bst:1099:FUNCTION {archiveprefix.or.eprinttype} % holder for eprinttype with archiveprefix precedence\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_natbib.bst:1128:            { journal } % if journal field is not empty, output it (takes precedence)\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/acl_lualatex.tex:8:% This is not strictly necessary, and may be commented out,\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/anthology.bib.txt:7:- `words` is the first significant word in the title, or more, if necessary,\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/README.md:29:make necessary changes. Minimally, you'll need to update the name of\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/formatting.md:69:Please make sure that your PDF file embeds all necessary fonts (especially for tree diagrams, symbols, and Asian languages).\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/formatting.md:237:If a piece of prior work appeared in multiple venues, the version that appeared in a refereed, archival venue should be referenced.\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/formatting.md:238:If multiple versions of a piece of prior work exist, the one used by the authors should be referenced.\ndocs/paper/_acl_template/formatting.md:296:Supplementary material may report preprocessing decisions, model parameters, and other details necessary for the replication of the experiments reported in the paper."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QM75A2yPEPSxtzHuseKCFN","session_id":"a13beb9d-44fb-4973-a348-fa71d68014d3","uuid":"66eeb34d-df44-4958-846d-a8d200d19afb","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:16:02.691Z"}
